Short:        A music format - PN-PokeyNoise.
Type:         mus/misc
Author:       achim.haertel@e-technik.tu-chemnitz.de (Achim Haertel)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

---

Deliplayer included
Freeware
Sourcecode included
Version 0.25

Thanks to Don Adan for improving the soundplaying

Note: The Deliplayer SFX recognizes sometimes PokeyNoise modules as SFX
and must be removed temporarily with the player management

---

Pokey is the soundchip found in the 8-bit Atari series of computers
- 400/800/XL/XE. The PokeyNoise DeliPlayer was written by Achim Haertel
in 1996 and never finished. The fileformat for these tunes is abit like
the old PlaySID format with an icon for each music file. Supports now
also SAP files type C, B and M (80% of ASMA collection) and includes a
music top list.
